            "review_title": "Review at Mon Hue Restaurant",
            "review_text": "David B\nRayong, Thailand9085 contributions\n0\nLet Down on Return Visit\nJan 2018 • Family\nI first ate at Mon Hue about four years ago and was delighted with the food, which features regional Hue specials, and the service. This visit was a big let down.\n\nTo begin with the first five dishes we ordered were no longer available, and we were early diners at 6 p.m. so i could see not any excuse for them no longer being available.\n\nWhen our food did come, in drips and drabs with no coordination of what we had ordered as a whole, the food was mediocre.\n\nOn top of that our waitress, who was a delightful, friendly young woman, could speak almost no English. We asked for \"plates\", which had not been provided and were greeted with a totally uncomprehending stare. The same with \"glasses\", \"spoons\" and \"toothpicks\".\n\nIt is not her fault that she does not speak English. It is the fault of management who have hired her and not taught her, for this is the epicenter of Saigon's tourist zones, and English is essential for any Vietnamese business.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten January 28, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-10",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
