            "review_text": "Jady O\nGeorge Town, Malaysia129 contributions\n0\nTasty Broth, but I think I saw something fishy...\nMay 2017 • Solo\nThis is not the Normal type of pho you have in Vietnam. First, the noodle is rounded instead of flat rice noodle used in \"laksa\". \n\nThen the soup comes with pork blood, hence do not be surprise to see the chunk of black pork blood even you order beef noodle. \n\nThe vege accompanied the noodle is kind of like fern or seaweed, not sure what it is but is in good texture. \n\nLastly the soup aka pho is delicious! \n\nBut when I about to go off, kinda saw the waiter combine 2 small bowl of leftover sauce into one, then give it to the next table... Kinda shock.\nRead more\nWritten May 4, 2017",
